<p>If you rent out concrete mixers, compactors, scaffolding or generators, HardPoint keeps the hire book for you: what's out, with whom,
  when it's due back and what they owe.</p>

<h2>Adding your tools</h2>
<ol>
  <li>Go to <strong>Settings › Tools for hire</strong> (owners, managers and whoever looks after the catalogue).</li>
  <li>Add each physical tool with its own asset tag (for example <code>MIX-01</code>), the branch it lives at, the daily rate, a weekly
    rate if you offer one, and the deposit you ask for.</li>
</ol>
<p>Once you have tools, <strong>Hire</strong> appears in the menu.</p>

<h2>Hiring out</h2>
<ol>
  <li>Press <strong>New hire</strong>, pick the customer (or add a new one) and note their ID number and where the tools are going.</li>
  <li>Tick the tools and set when they're due back. HardPoint shows an estimate of the charges.</li>
  <li>On the hire, press <strong>Take deposit</strong> (cash goes into the till drawer, or M-Pesa or card) and <strong>Print agreement</strong> for the customer to sign.</li>
</ol>

<h2>While tools are out</h2>
<ul>
  <li>The <strong>Overdue</strong> tab shows hires past their due time. <strong>Text a reminder</strong> sends the customer a text (at most once a day, where SMS is on).</li>
  <li><strong>Extend</strong> moves the due-back time when the customer calls to keep the tools longer.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Returns and charges</h2>
<p>Press <strong>Tools back</strong> and tick what's come back. Tools can come back on different days. Add a note on condition and a damage
  charge if needed; tick <strong>Needs repair before it goes out again</strong> to send the tool to maintenance instead of back to available.</p>
<p>A day is 24 hours from when the tool went out, with an hour's grace, so a mixer out at 9am and back by 10am the next day is one day. Where a
  tool has a weekly rate, a week never costs more than that rate.</p>

<h2>Settling up</h2>
<p>When everything is back, open the till and press <strong>Settle … at this till</strong> on the hire. The hire charges appear as lines on the sale, the deposit
  counts towards them, and the customer pays any balance. If the deposit was more than the charges, press <strong>Refund</strong> on the hire to give the rest back.</p>
